  "measurement_interpretation": [
    "Each workload offers 200 operations over 20 seconds after five seconds of warmup; all submitted operations, 36 replicas and final archive cuts reconcile in each run.",
    "Generator rejections are retained in the offered-load error fraction. Both runs miss the declared local traffic objectives.",
    "Cross-node operation sums cover staggered sampling windows and overlap in time. Engine persist includes engine sync; elapsed sums cannot be added into CPU time or a critical-path attribution.",
    "Object failed-response counts include conditional conflicts and are not business-command failure counts. Requested PUT bytes are not confirmed durability. Socket endpoint sums double-count traffic when read and write totals are combined.",
    "The local workload reads followers through public HTTP, so the peer query-lane byte count can be zero. The healthy runner does not enable the automatic repair controller; its zero attempt counts do not measure repair performance.",
    "The image and deployed executable were verified against all copied source inputs before each run. Only plan/evidence files were uncommitted; production source is pinned.",
    "Quorum and S3 acknowledgements have different durability contracts and cannot establish an equivalent speedup. Other host workloads and swap were uncontrolled; no comparison with older runs establishes causality."
  ],
